  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $F$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $F$ where every element of $F$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{a},{b},{c},{d},{e}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{a},{b,e},{b},{c,d}}$ is not a partition because the elements $b$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{a,b,e},{c,d,f}}$ is not a partition because the element $f$ does not appear in $F.$\n\n- ${\u2205,{a,b,c,d,e}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{a,b},{c,d}}$ is not a partition because the element $e\\in F$ does not appear in any subset.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
